{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-inductive-gb-reduction","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:inductive-gb-reduction","kind":"proposition","title":"Inductive Gröbner--Shirshov reduction","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-derived-atom"],"tags":["groebner-shirshov","inductive","normal-form","hecke-algebra"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Interactions.inductiveGBReduction","text":"inductive-gb-reduction.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:inductive-gb-reduction\"></a><p>We compute the nuclear normal form inductively by reducing intermediate words after each multiplication.</p>\n<p><strong>Proposition.</strong>\n<em>The inductive step yields a normal form containing at most <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom{A-1}{\\lfloor(A-1)/2\\rfloor}</code> terms.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/inductive-gb-reduction.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"11.1.5"}
